On Fri, Jul 22, 2011 at 11:38 PM, John E. Clifford <kali9putra@yahoo.com> wrote:
> There are many cases where that simple approach doesn't work satisfactorily, mainly with longer scopes or more buried ones.

I'm not aware of any such cases, at least as long as we are talking
about quantifiers, logical connectives and negation. If you are
talking about some other ill defined operators, we may not have
everything worked out, but for those basic three types the translation
of any Lojban sentence into logical notation can be done in a
completely mechanical way.

